  ('3709', 2024, 'allowance', 'Uniform allowance ordinary clothes', 'active', '3759', '3709/3759', NULL, NULL, 'SARS PAYE BRS - PAYE Employer Reconciliation V22.1.2 (effective 1 March 2023; PDF sha256 e3f915d0825e7a48a778df0f3b85031dc4e184693438234eb58bfd2a3a21649f); row text carried from the SARS PAYE-AE-06-G06 (Guide for Codes Applicable to Employees Tax Certificates 2026) 2026 list (no change in meaning for this code)', 'https://www.sars.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/Docs/PAYE/BRS/SARS_PAYE_BRS-PAYE-Employer-Reconciliation_V22-1-2.pdf', '• An allowance for a special uniform, which is clearly distinguishable from . (Non-taxable) Note: ▫ Use code 3759 ONLY for foreign services income. ▫ The value of this code must be included in the value of code 3714/3764 with effect from the 2010 year of assessment.', 'v22.1.2'),
  ('3710', 2024, 'allowance', 'Tool allowance (PAYE)', 'active', '3760', '3710/3760', NULL, NULL, 'SARS PAYE BRS - PAYE Employer Reconciliation V22.1.2 (effective 1 March 2023; PDF sha256 e3f915d0825e7a48a778df0f3b85031dc4e184693438234eb58bfd2a3a21649f); row text carried from the SARS PAYE-AE-06-G06 (Guide for Codes Applicable to Employees Tax Certificates 2026) 2026 list (no change in meaning for this code)', 'https://www.sars.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/Docs/PAYE/BRS/SARS_PAYE_BRS-PAYE-Employer-Reconciliation_V22-1-2.pdf', '• An allowance for the acquisition of tools for business use. PAYE) Note: ▫ Use code 3760 ONLY for foreign services income. ▫ The value of this code must be included in the value of code 3713/3763 with effect from the 2010 year of assessment.', 'v22.1.2'),
  ('3711', 2024, 'allowance', 'Computer allowance', 'active', '3761', '3711/3761', NULL, NULL, 'SARS PAYE BRS - PAYE Employer Reconciliation V22.1.2 (effective 1 March 2023; PDF sha256 e3f915d0825e7a48a778df0f3b85031dc4e184693438234eb58bfd2a3a21649f); row text carried from the SARS PAYE-AE-06-G06 (Guide for Codes Applicable to Employees Tax Certificates 2026) 2026 list (no change in meaning for this code)', 'https://www.sars.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/Docs/PAYE/BRS/SARS_PAYE_BRS-PAYE-Employer-Reconciliation_V22-1-2.pdf', '• An allowance for the acquisition or use of a computer. (Subject to Note: PAYE) ▫ Use code 3761 ONLY for foreign services income; ▫ The value of this code must be included in the value of code 3713/3763 with effect from the 2010 year of assessment. Effective Date: 19 September 2025', 'v22.1.2'),
  ('3712', 2024, 'allowance', 'Telephone/cell phone allowance for business purposes', 'active', '3762', '3712/3762', NULL, NULL, 'SARS PAYE BRS - PAYE Employer Reconciliation V22.1.2 (effective 1 March 2023; PDF sha256 e3f915d0825e7a48a778df0f3b85031dc4e184693438234eb58bfd2a3a21649f); row text carried from the SARS PAYE-AE-06-G06 (Guide for Codes Applicable to Employees Tax Certificates 2026) 2026 list (no change in meaning for this code)', 'https://www.sars.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/Docs/PAYE/BRS/SARS_PAYE_BRS-PAYE-Employer-Reconciliation_V22-1-2.pdf', '• An allowance for expenses incurred in the use of a telephone/cell phone . (Subject to PAYE) Note: ▫ Use code 3762 ONLY for foreign services income; ▫ The value of this code must be included in the value of code 3713/3763 with effect from the 2010 year of assessment.', 'v22.1.2'),
  ('3713', 2024, 'allowance', 'Other allowances', 'active', '3763', '3713/3763', NULL, 'incorporated into 3713/3763. Codes 3705/3755 and 3709/3759 and 3716/3766 must be incorporated into', 'SARS PAYE BRS - PAYE Employer Reconciliation V22.1.2 (effective 1 March 2023; PDF sha256 e3f915d0825e7a48a778df0f3b85031dc4e184693438234eb58bfd2a3a21649f); row text carried from the SARS PAYE-AE-06-G06 (Guide for Codes Applicable to Employees Tax Certificates 2026) 2026 list (no change in meaning for this code)', 'https://www.sars.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/Docs/PAYE/BRS/SARS_PAYE_BRS-PAYE-Employer-Reconciliation_V22-1-2.pdf', '• All other allowances, which do not comply with any of the descriptions (Subject to listed under allowances, must be added together and reflected under this PAYE) code on the certificate. • Examples include: ▫ Any subsistence allowances/advances paid to an employee during any month which is deemed to be remuneration by the end of the next month due to the employee not spending the night away from his/her residence or has not refunded the allowance/advance to the employer ▫ If an employer allows', 'v22.1.2'),
  ('3714', 2024, 'allowance', 'Other allowances descriptions listed under allowances, must be added together, and (Non-taxable)', 'active', '3764', '3714/3764', NULL, '.', 'SARS PAYE BRS - PAYE Employer Reconciliation V22.1.2 (effective 1 March 2023; PDF sha256 e3f915d0825e7a48a778df0f3b85031dc4e184693438234eb58bfd2a3a21649f); row text carried from the SARS PAYE-AE-06-G06 (Guide for Codes Applicable to Employees Tax Certificates 2026) 2026 list (no change in meaning for this code)', 'https://www.sars.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/Docs/PAYE/BRS/SARS_PAYE_BRS-PAYE-Employer-Reconciliation_V22-1-2.pdf', '• All other non-taxable allowances, which do not comply with any of the reflected under this code on the certificate. • Examples include: ▫ Non-taxable Relocation allowance; ▫ Non-taxable Subsistence allowance for local and foreign travel not exceeding the daily limits; ▫ Non-taxable allowance for a uniform which is clearly distinguishable from ordinary clothing. Note: ▫ Use code 3764 ONLY for foreign services income; ▫ With effect from 2010 year of assessment, amounts previously included under', 'v22.1.2'),
  ('3715', 2024, 'allowance', 'Subsistence allowance – costs for foreign travel, which exceeds the deemed amounts', 'active', '3765', '3715/3765', NULL, NULL, 'SARS PAYE BRS - PAYE Employer Reconciliation V22.1.2 (effective 1 March 2023; PDF sha256 e3f915d0825e7a48a778df0f3b85031dc4e184693438234eb58bfd2a3a21649f); row text carried from the SARS PAYE-AE-06-G06 (Guide for Codes Applicable to Employees Tax Certificates 2026) 2026 list (no change in meaning for this code)', 'https://www.sars.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/Docs/PAYE/BRS/SARS_PAYE_BRS-PAYE-Employer-Reconciliation_V22-1-2.pdf', '• An allowance paid for expenses in respect of meals and/or incidental . foreign travel (IT) Note: ▫ Use code 3765 ONLY for foreign services income.', 'v22.1.2'),
  ('3716', 2024, 'allowance', 'Subsistence', 'active', '3766', '3716/3766', NULL, NULL, 'SARS PAYE BRS - PAYE Employer Reconciliation V22.1.2 (effective 1 March 2023; PDF sha256 e3f915d0825e7a48a778df0f3b85031dc4e184693438234eb58bfd2a3a21649f); row text carried from the SARS PAYE-AE-06-G06 (Guide for Codes Applicable to Employees Tax Certificates 2026) 2026 list (no change in meaning for this code)', 'https://www.sars.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/Docs/PAYE/BRS/SARS_PAYE_BRS-PAYE-Employer-Reconciliation_V22-1-2.pdf', '• An allowance paid for expenses in respect of meals and/or incidental allowance – costs for foreign travel, which does not exceed the deemed amounts. foreign travel (Non-taxable) Note: ▫ Use code 3766 ONLY for foreign services income; ▫ The value of this code must be included in the value of code 3714/3764 with effect from the 2010 year of assessment.', 'v22.1.2'),
  ('3717', 2024, 'allowance', 'Broad-based', 'active', '3767', '3717/3767', NULL, NULL, 'SARS PAYE BRS - PAYE Employer Reconciliation V22.1.2 (effective 1 March 2023; PDF sha256 e3f915d0825e7a48a778df0f3b85031dc4e184693438234eb58bfd2a3a21649f); row text carried from the SARS PAYE-AE-06-G06 (Guide for Codes Applicable to Employees Tax Certificates 2026) 2026 list (no change in meaning for this code)', 'https://www.sars.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/Docs/PAYE/BRS/SARS_PAYE_BRS-PAYE-Employer-Reconciliation_V22-1-2.pdf', '• An amount received/accrued from the disposal of any qualifying equity employee share share or any right of interest in a qualifying equity share in terms of plan certain conditions. (Subject to PAYE) Note: ▫ Use code 3767 ONLY for foreign services income.', 'v22.1.2'),
  ('3718', 2024, 'allowance', 'Vesting of equity', 'active', '3768', '3718/3768', NULL, NULL, 'SARS PAYE BRS - PAYE Employer Reconciliation V22.1.2 (effective 1 March 2023; PDF sha256 e3f915d0825e7a48a778df0f3b85031dc4e184693438234eb58bfd2a3a21649f); row text carried from the SARS PAYE-AE-06-G06 (Guide for Codes Applicable to Employees Tax Certificates 2026) 2026 list (no change in meaning for this code)', 'https://www.sars.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/Docs/PAYE/BRS/SARS_PAYE_BRS-PAYE-Employer-Reconciliation_V22-1-2.pdf', '• Any amount in respect of the vesting of any equity instrument or the instruments or return of capital in respect of restricted equity instruments (section 8C). return of capital iron. restricted Note: equity ▫ A return of capital received by or accrued to an employee in respect instruments of restricted equity instruments on or after 8 January 2016 (during the (PAYE) 2016 year of assessment) is liable for PAYE and should be included under this code. ▫ Use code 3768 ONLY for foreign services in', 'v22.1.2'),
  ('3719', 2024, 'allowance', 'Dividends not exempt i.r.o. par (dd) of the proviso to s10(1)(k)(i) (PAYE)', 'conditional', '3769', '3719/3769', 'Applicable from the 2018 year of assessment | applicable from 2018 year of assessment', 'Applicable from the 2018 year of assessment', 'SARS PAYE BRS - PAYE Employer Reconciliation V22.1.2 (effective 1 March 2023; PDF sha256 e3f915d0825e7a48a778df0f3b85031dc4e184693438234eb58bfd2a3a21649f); row text carried from the SARS PAYE-AE-06-G06 (Guide for Codes Applicable to Employees Tax Certificates 2026) 2026 list (no change in meaning for this code)', 'https://www.sars.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/Docs/PAYE/BRS/SARS_PAYE_BRS-PAYE-Employer-Reconciliation_V22-1-2.pdf', '• Dividends in respect of restricted equity instrument as defined in section .e. para 8C to the extent that the restricted equity instrument was acquired in (dd) of the circumstances contemplated in section 8C. However, the dividends in proviso to respect of any of the following equity instruments are excluded from s10(1)(k)(i) “remuneration” under code 3719. (PAYE) ▫ The restricted equity instrument s an equity shares other than an equity share that would have constituted a hybrid equity instru', 'v22.1.2'),
  ('3720', 2024, 'allowance', 'Dividends not exempt i.r.o. par (ii) of the proviso to s10(1)(k)(i) (PAYE)', 'conditional', '3770', '3720/3770', 'Applicable from the 2018 year of assessment | applicable from 2018 year of assessment', 'Applicable from the 2018 year of assessment', 'SARS PAYE BRS - PAYE Employer Reconciliation V22.1.2 (effective 1 March 2023; PDF sha256 e3f915d0825e7a48a778df0f3b85031dc4e184693438234eb58bfd2a3a21649f); row text carried from the SARS PAYE-AE-06-G06 (Guide for Codes Applicable to Employees Tax Certificates 2026) 2026 list (no change in meaning for this code)', 'https://www.sars.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/Docs/PAYE/BRS/SARS_PAYE_BRS-PAYE-Employer-Reconciliation_V22-1-2.pdf', '• Any dividend received by or accrued to a person in respect of services .e. par (ii) rendered or to be rendered or in respect of or by virtue of employment or of the proviso to the holding of any office, other than a dividend received or accrued in s10(1)(k)(i) respect of a restricted equity instrument as defined in section 8C held by (PAYE) that person or in respect of a share held by that person. Note: ▫ Use code 3770 ONLY for local dividends linked to foreign services. ▫ Only applicable from', 'v22.1.2'),
  ('3721', 2024, 'allowance', 'Dividends not exempt i.r.o. par (jj) of the proviso to s10(1)(k)(i) (PAYE)', 'conditional', '3771', '3721/3771', 'Applicable from the 2018 year of assessment | applicable from 2018 year of assessment', 'Applicable from the 2018 year of assessment', 'SARS PAYE BRS - PAYE Employer Reconciliation V22.1.2 (effective 1 March 2023; PDF sha256 e3f915d0825e7a48a778df0f3b85031dc4e184693438234eb58bfd2a3a21649f); row text carried from the SARS PAYE-AE-06-G06 (Guide for Codes Applicable to Employees Tax Certificates 2026) 2026 list (no change in meaning for this code)', 'https://www.sars.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/Docs/PAYE/BRS/SARS_PAYE_BRS-PAYE-Employer-Reconciliation_V22-1-2.pdf', '• Any dividend in respect of a restricted equity instrument as defined in .e. par (jj) section 8C that was acquired in the circumstances contemplated in of the proviso to s section 8C if that dividend is derived directly or indirectly from, or 10(1)( k)(i) constitutes – (PAYE) ▫ An amount transferred or applied by a company as consideration for the acquisition or redemption of any share in that company; ▫ An amount received or accrued in anticipation or during the winding up, liquidation, deregi', 'v22.1.2'),
  ('3722', 2024, 'allowance', 'Reimbursive travel allowance (PAYE)', 'conditional', '3772', '3722/3772', 'Applicable from the 2019 year of assessment | applicable from 2019 year of assessment', 'Applicable from the 2019 year of assessment', 'SARS PAYE BRS - PAYE Employer Reconciliation V22.1.2 (effective 1 March 2023; PDF sha256 e3f915d0825e7a48a778df0f3b85031dc4e184693438234eb58bfd2a3a21649f); row text carried from the SARS PAYE-AE-06-G06 (Guide for Codes Applicable to Employees Tax Certificates 2026) 2026 list (no change in meaning for this code)', 'https://www.sars.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/Docs/PAYE/BRS/SARS_PAYE_BRS-PAYE-Employer-Reconciliation_V22-1-2.pdf', 'travel allowance • The reimbursement rate used by the employer exceeds the prescribed rate (paragraph 4 of the Fixing of Rate per Kilometre i.e., Motor Vehicle Regulation) and only in respect of that portion that EXCEEDS the amount determined by multiplying the prescribed rate by the actual business kilometres travelled. Note 1: From 2019 year of assessment, use the prescribed rate applicable to the relevant year of assessment. EXAMPLE: • If the prescribed rate is R3.61/km and the employer reimb', 'v22.1.2'),
  ('3723', 2024, 'allowance', 'Dividends not exempt i.r.o. par (kk) of the proviso to s10(1)(k)(i) (PAYE)', 'conditional', '3773', '3723/3773', 'Applicable from the 2018 year of assessment | applicable from 2018 year of assessment', 'Applicable from the 2018 year of assessment', 'SARS PAYE BRS - PAYE Employer Reconciliation V22.1.2 (effective 1 March 2023; PDF sha256 e3f915d0825e7a48a778df0f3b85031dc4e184693438234eb58bfd2a3a21649f); row text carried from the SARS PAYE-AE-06-G06 (Guide for Codes Applicable to Employees Tax Certificates 2026) 2026 list (no change in meaning for this code)', 'https://www.sars.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/Docs/PAYE/BRS/SARS_PAYE_BRS-PAYE-Employer-Reconciliation_V22-1-2.pdf', 'exempt i.e. par section 8C that was acquired in the circumstances contemplated in section (kk) of the proviso 8C(1) if that dividend is derived directly or indirectly from: to s10(1)(k)(i) • An amount transferred or applied by a company as consideration for the (PAYE) acquisition or redemption of any share in that company, or • Any amount received or accrued in anticipation or during the winding up, liquidation or final termination of a company. Note: ▫ Use code 3773 ONLY for local dividends lin', 'v22.1.2'),
  ('3724', 2024, 'allowance', 'Amounts paid by any COVID-19 Disaster Relief Organisation (IT)', 'deprecated', NULL, '3724', 'Only applicable for the 2021 year of assessment | only applicable for 2021 year of assessment', 'Only applicable for the 2021 year of assessment', 'SARS PAYE BRS - PAYE Employer Reconciliation V22.1.2 (effective 1 March 2023; PDF sha256 e3f915d0825e7a48a778df0f3b85031dc4e184693438234eb58bfd2a3a21649f); row text carried from the SARS PAYE-AE-06-G06 (Guide for Codes Applicable to Employees Tax Certificates 2026) 2026 list (no change in meaning for this code)', 'https://www.sars.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/Docs/PAYE/BRS/SARS_PAYE_BRS-PAYE-Employer-Reconciliation_V22-1-2.pdf', 'any COVID-19 Organisation (so called section 18A Relief scheme / fund) and paid to an Disaster Relief employee. Organisation (IT) Note: ▫ This code must not be used for benefits received from UIF Temporary Employees Relief Scheme (UIF TERS). ▫ This code is only applicable for 2021 year of assessment. Effective Date: 19 September 2025', 'v22.1.2'),
