  ('3703', 2025, 'allowance', 'Reimbursive travel allowance (Excl)', 'conditional', '3753', '3703/3753', 'applicable from 2019 year of', NULL, 'SARS PAYE BRS - PAYE Employer Reconciliation V23.0.0 (effective 1 March 2024; PDF sha256 220bf3ac4e13f5ffb0e8f4d090071db1babdcfec2425c5c5526d74d509e350ca); row text carried from the SARS PAYE-AE-06-G06 (Guide for Codes Applicable to Employees Tax Certificates 2026) 2026 list (no change in meaning for this code)', 'https://www.sars.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/Docs/PAYE/BRS/SARS_PAYE_BRS-PAYE-Employer-Reconciliation_V23-0-0.pdf', 'travel allowance • The reimbursement rate used by the employer does not exceed the (Non-taxable) prescribed rate (paragraph 4 of the Fixing of Rate per Kilometre i.e., Motor Vehicle Regulation) and / or • The employee does not receive any other form of compensation for travel and in respect of the full value of the reimbursement. Note 2: EXAMPLE- • If the prescribed rate is R3.61 /km and the employer reimbursed employee at R3.50km for 12540 business km’s travelled during the 2019 year of assessm', 'v23.0.0'),
