  ('3712', 2025, 'allowance', 'Telephone/cell phone allowance for business purposes', 'active', '3762', '3712/3762', NULL, NULL, 'SARS PAYE BRS - PAYE Employer Reconciliation V23.0.0 (effective 1 March 2024; PDF sha256 220bf3ac4e13f5ffb0e8f4d090071db1babdcfec2425c5c5526d74d509e350ca); row text carried from the SARS PAYE-AE-06-G06 (Guide for Codes Applicable to Employees Tax Certificates 2026) 2026 list (no change in meaning for this code)', 'https://www.sars.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/Docs/PAYE/BRS/SARS_PAYE_BRS-PAYE-Employer-Reconciliation_V23-0-0.pdf', '• An allowance for expenses incurred in the use of a telephone/cell phone . (Subject to PAYE) Note: ▫ Use code 3762 ONLY for foreign services income; ▫ The value of this code must be included in the value of code 3713/3763 with effect from the 2010 year of assessment.', 'v23.0.0'),
  ('3713', 2025, 'allowance', 'Other allowances', 'active', '3763', '3713/3763', NULL, 'incorporated into 3713/3763. Codes 3705/3755 and 3709/3759 and 3716/3766 must be incorporated into', 'SARS PAYE BRS - PAYE Employer Reconciliation V23.0.0 (effective 1 March 2024; PDF sha256 220bf3ac4e13f5ffb0e8f4d090071db1babdcfec2425c5c5526d74d509e350ca); row text carried from the SARS PAYE-AE-06-G06 (Guide for Codes Applicable to Employees Tax Certificates 2026) 2026 list (no change in meaning for this code)', 'https://www.sars.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/Docs/PAYE/BRS/SARS_PAYE_BRS-PAYE-Employer-Reconciliation_V23-0-0.pdf', '• All other allowances, which do not comply with any of the descriptions (Subject to listed under allowances, must be added together and reflected under this PAYE) code on the certificate. • Examples include: ▫ Any subsistence allowances/advances paid to an employee during any month which is deemed to be remuneration by the end of the next month due to the employee not spending the night away from his/her residence or has not refunded the allowance/advance to the employer ▫ If an employer allows', 'v23.0.0'),
  ('3714', 2025, 'allowance', 'Other allowances descriptions listed under allowances, must be added together, and (Non-taxable)', 'active', '3764', '3714/3764', NULL, '.', 'SARS PAYE BRS - PAYE Employer Reconciliation V23.0.0 (effective 1 March 2024; PDF sha256 220bf3ac4e13f5ffb0e8f4d090071db1babdcfec2425c5c5526d74d509e350ca); row text carried from the SARS PAYE-AE-06-G06 (Guide for Codes Applicable to Employees Tax Certificates 2026) 2026 list (no change in meaning for this code)', 'https://www.sars.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/Docs/PAYE/BRS/SARS_PAYE_BRS-PAYE-Employer-Reconciliation_V23-0-0.pdf', '• All other non-taxable allowances, which do not comply with any of the reflected under this code on the certificate. • Examples include: ▫ Non-taxable Relocation allowance; ▫ Non-taxable Subsistence allowance for local and foreign travel not exceeding the daily limits; ▫ Non-taxable allowance for a uniform which is clearly distinguishable from ordinary clothing. Note: ▫ Use code 3764 ONLY for foreign services income; ▫ With effect from 2010 year of assessment, amounts previously included under', 'v23.0.0'),
  ('3715', 2025, 'allowance', 'Subsistence allowance – costs for foreign travel, which exceeds the deemed amounts', 'active', '3765', '3715/3765', NULL, NULL, 'SARS PAYE BRS - PAYE Employer Reconciliation V23.0.0 (effective 1 March 2024; PDF sha256 220bf3ac4e13f5ffb0e8f4d090071db1babdcfec2425c5c5526d74d509e350ca); row text carried from the SARS PAYE-AE-06-G06 (Guide for Codes Applicable to Employees Tax Certificates 2026) 2026 list (no change in meaning for this code)', 'https://www.sars.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/Docs/PAYE/BRS/SARS_PAYE_BRS-PAYE-Employer-Reconciliation_V23-0-0.pdf', '• An allowance paid for expenses in respect of meals and/or incidental . foreign travel (IT) Note: ▫ Use code 3765 ONLY for foreign services income.', 'v23.0.0'),
