  ('3835', 2025, 'fringe', 'Long Service Award', 'conditional', '3885', '3835/3885', 'Only applicable from the 2023 year of assessment | applicable from the 2023 year of assessment | Valid from 2023 year of assessment', 'Only applicable from the 2023 year of assessment', 'SARS PAYE BRS - PAYE Employer Reconciliation V23.0.0 (effective 1 March 2024; PDF sha256 220bf3ac4e13f5ffb0e8f4d090071db1babdcfec2425c5c5526d74d509e350ca); row text carried from the SARS PAYE-AE-06-G06 (Guide for Codes Applicable to Employees Tax Certificates 2026) 2026 list (no change in meaning for this code)', 'https://www.sars.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/Docs/PAYE/BRS/SARS_PAYE_BRS-PAYE-Employer-Reconciliation_V23-0-0.pdf', '• A Long Service Award given to an employee that complies with the initial unbroken period of service of not less than 15 years or any subsequent unbroken period of service of not less than 10 years. Note: ▫ The full value (before excluding any amount) of a Long Service Award consisting of taxable benefits referred to below, that qualify for R5,000 exclusion must be declared under this code. ▫ Long Service means an initial unbroken period of service not less than 15 years or any subsequent unbro', 'v23.0.0'),
  ('3901', 2025, 'lump_sum', 'Gratuities / Severance', 'active', '3951', '3901/3951', NULL, NULL, 'SARS PAYE BRS - PAYE Employer Reconciliation V23.0.0 (effective 1 March 2024; PDF sha256 220bf3ac4e13f5ffb0e8f4d090071db1babdcfec2425c5c5526d74d509e350ca); row text carried from the SARS PAYE-AE-06-G06 (Guide for Codes Applicable to Employees Tax Certificates 2026) 2026 list (no change in meaning for this code)', 'https://www.sars.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/Docs/PAYE/BRS/SARS_PAYE_BRS-PAYE-Employer-Reconciliation_V23-0-0.pdf', '• Gratuities paid/payable by an employer prior to 1 March 2011. Benefits • Severance benefits, as defined, paid/payable by an employer after 1 March (Subject to 2011, if employee: PAYE) ▫ Is 55 years or older; ▫ Became permanently incapable to be employed due to ill health, etc.; or ▫ Services terminated due to reduction of personnel or employer ceased trading. Note: ▫ A lump sum paid/payable in terms of par (d) of “gross income” which is not a ‘severance benefit,’ MUST be reflected under code 3', 'v23.0.0'),
  ('3902', 2025, 'lump_sum', 'Pension / RAF (PAYE) – withdrawal, accruing prior to 1 March 2009', 'active', '3952', '3902/3952', NULL, NULL, 'SARS PAYE BRS - PAYE Employer Reconciliation V23.0.0 (effective 1 March 2024; PDF sha256 220bf3ac4e13f5ffb0e8f4d090071db1babdcfec2425c5c5526d74d509e350ca); row text carried from the SARS PAYE-AE-06-G06 (Guide for Codes Applicable to Employees Tax Certificates 2026) 2026 list (no change in meaning for this code)', 'https://www.sars.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/Docs/PAYE/BRS/SARS_PAYE_BRS-PAYE-Employer-Reconciliation_V23-0-0.pdf', '• Lump sum accruing prior to 1 March 2009 from a Pension/Retirement annuity .g., resignation, transfer, surplus PAYE) apportionment, etc.), including ‘Unclaimed benefits’ only claimed and paid to a member of a Pension fund from 1 March 2009. Note: ▫ Use code 3952 ONLY for foreign services income; ▫ The value of this code must be included in the value of code 3920 or 3921 (where applicable) with effect from the 2010 year of assessment - i.e. only if the date of accrual is from 1 March 2009).', 'v23.0.0'),
  ('3903', 2025, 'lump_sum', 'Pension / RAF (PAYE) – retirement or death, accruing prior to 1 October 2007', 'conditional', '3953', '3903/3953', 'valid from 2009 year of assessment', NULL, 'SARS PAYE BRS - PAYE Employer Reconciliation V23.0.0 (effective 1 March 2024; PDF sha256 220bf3ac4e13f5ffb0e8f4d090071db1babdcfec2425c5c5526d74d509e350ca); row text carried from the SARS PAYE-AE-06-G06 (Guide for Codes Applicable to Employees Tax Certificates 2026) 2026 list (no change in meaning for this code)', 'https://www.sars.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/Docs/PAYE/BRS/SARS_PAYE_BRS-PAYE-Employer-Reconciliation_V23-0-0.pdf', '• Lump sum payments accruing prior to 1 October 2007 from a Pension / . PAYE) Note: ▫ Use code 3953 ONLY for foreign services income; ▫ This code is invalid from 2009 year of assessment. ▫ The value of this code must be included in the value of code 3915 with effect from the 2009 year of assessment.', 'v23.0.0'),
  ('3904', 2025, 'lump_sum', 'Provident (PAYE) – withdrawal, accruing prior to 1 March 2009', 'active', '3954', '3904/3954', NULL, NULL, 'SARS PAYE BRS - PAYE Employer Reconciliation V23.0.0 (effective 1 March 2024; PDF sha256 220bf3ac4e13f5ffb0e8f4d090071db1babdcfec2425c5c5526d74d509e350ca); row text carried from the SARS PAYE-AE-06-G06 (Guide for Codes Applicable to Employees Tax Certificates 2026) 2026 list (no change in meaning for this code)', 'https://www.sars.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/Docs/PAYE/BRS/SARS_PAYE_BRS-PAYE-Employer-Reconciliation_V23-0-0.pdf', '• Lump sum accruing prior to 1 March 2009 from a Provident fund lump sum in PAYE) including ‘Unclaimed benefits’ only claimed and paid to a member of a Provident fund from 1 March 2009. Note: ▫ Use code 3954 ONLY for foreign services income; ▫ The value of this code must be included in the value of code 3920 or 3921 (where applicable) with effect from the 2010 year of assessment - i.e. only if the date of accrual is from 1 March 2009).', 'v23.0.0'),
  ('3905', 2025, 'lump_sum', 'Provident (PAYE) – retirement or death, accruing prior to 1 October 2007', 'conditional', '3955', '3905/3955', 'valid from 2009 year of assessment', NULL, 'SARS PAYE BRS - PAYE Employer Reconciliation V23.0.0 (effective 1 March 2024; PDF sha256 220bf3ac4e13f5ffb0e8f4d090071db1babdcfec2425c5c5526d74d509e350ca); row text carried from the SARS PAYE-AE-06-G06 (Guide for Codes Applicable to Employees Tax Certificates 2026) 2026 list (no change in meaning for this code)', 'https://www.sars.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/Docs/PAYE/BRS/SARS_PAYE_BRS-PAYE-Employer-Reconciliation_V23-0-0.pdf', '• Lump sum payments accruing prior to 1 October 2007 from a Provident fund . PAYE) Note: ▫ Use code 3955 ONLY for foreign services income; ▫ This code is invalid from 2009 year of assessment. ▫ The value of this code must be included in the value of code 3915 with effect from the 2009 year of assessment.', 'v23.0.0'),
  ('3906', 2025, 'lump_sum', 'Special Remuneration', 'active', '3956', '3906/3956', NULL, '3901/3951', 'SARS PAYE BRS - PAYE Employer Reconciliation V23.0.0 (effective 1 March 2024; PDF sha256 220bf3ac4e13f5ffb0e8f4d090071db1babdcfec2425c5c5526d74d509e350ca); row text carried from the SARS PAYE-AE-06-G06 (Guide for Codes Applicable to Employees Tax Certificates 2026) 2026 list (no change in meaning for this code)', 'https://www.sars.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/Docs/PAYE/BRS/SARS_PAYE_BRS-PAYE-Employer-Reconciliation_V23-0-0.pdf', '• Special remuneration paid to proto-team members. (Subject to Note: PAYE) ▫ Use code 3956 ONLY for foreign services income. Effective Date: 19 September 2025 Description Explanation', 'v23.0.0'),
  ('3907', 2025, 'lump_sum', 'Other lump sums (PAYE)', 'active', '3957', '3907/3957', NULL, NULL, 'SARS PAYE BRS - PAYE Employer Reconciliation V23.0.0 (effective 1 March 2024; PDF sha256 220bf3ac4e13f5ffb0e8f4d090071db1babdcfec2425c5c5526d74d509e350ca); row text carried from the SARS PAYE-AE-06-G06 (Guide for Codes Applicable to Employees Tax Certificates 2026) 2026 list (no change in meaning for this code)', 'https://www.sars.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/Docs/PAYE/BRS/SARS_PAYE_BRS-PAYE-Employer-Reconciliation_V23-0-0.pdf', '• Other lump sum payments. to PAYE) • Examples include: ▫ A lump sum payment paid/payable by an employer due to normal termination of service (e.g., resignation or retirement), which is NOT a ‘severance benefit,’ ▫ “Antedated salary/pension’ extending over previous years of assessment, for years of assessment prior to 2025. From 2025 year of assessment, this lump sum must be reflected under source code 3623/3673. Note: Use the original directive code, and do not resubmit previously submitted EMP', 'v23.0.0'),
  ('3908', 2025, 'lump_sum', 'Exempt Policy', 'conditional', NULL, '3908', 'Only applicable from the 2006 year of assessment | applicable from the 2006 year of assessment | Applicable from 1 March 2015', 'Only applicable from the 2006 year of assessment', 'SARS PAYE BRS - PAYE Employer Reconciliation V23.0.0 (effective 1 March 2024; PDF sha256 220bf3ac4e13f5ffb0e8f4d090071db1babdcfec2425c5c5526d74d509e350ca); row text carried from the SARS PAYE-AE-06-G06 (Guide for Codes Applicable to Employees Tax Certificates 2026) 2026 list (no change in meaning for this code)', 'https://www.sars.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/Docs/PAYE/BRS/SARS_PAYE_BRS-PAYE-Employer-Reconciliation_V23-0-0.pdf', '• Surplus apportionments on or after 1 January 2006 and before 1 March 2012 Proceeds (Non- paid in terms of section 15B of the Pension Funds Act of 1956. taxable) • Proceeds paid from an employer owned insurance policy exempt i.e., section 10(1)(gG) of the Income Tax Act - where the employer premiums were included as a taxable benefit in the employee’s income since the date contemplated in section 10(1)(gG) – see explanation under code 3907 (3957)– proceeds paid from an employer owned policy. •', 'v23.0.0'),
  ('3909', 2025, 'lump_sum', 'Unclaimed benefits (PAYE)', 'conditional', NULL, '3909', 'Only applicable from the 2007 to 2009 year of assessment | applicable from the 2007 to 2009 year of assessment | applicable from 2007 to 2009 year of assessment', 'Only applicable from the 2007 to 2009 year of assessment', 'SARS PAYE BRS - PAYE Employer Reconciliation V23.0.0 (effective 1 March 2024; PDF sha256 220bf3ac4e13f5ffb0e8f4d090071db1babdcfec2425c5c5526d74d509e350ca); row text carried from the SARS PAYE-AE-06-G06 (Guide for Codes Applicable to Employees Tax Certificates 2026) 2026 list (no change in meaning for this code)', 'https://www.sars.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/Docs/PAYE/BRS/SARS_PAYE_BRS-PAYE-Employer-Reconciliation_V23-0-0.pdf', '• Unclaimed benefits identified prior to 1 March 2009 and PAYE paid by the benefits fund but the benefit was not claimed by the member (General Note 35). (Subject to PAYE) Note: ▫ This code is only applicable from 2007 to 2009 year of assessment. Effective Date: 19 September 2025 Description Explanation', 'v23.0.0'),
  ('3915', 2025, 'lump_sum', 'Retirement /', 'conditional', NULL, '3915', 'Only applicable from the 2008 year of assessment | applicable from the 2008 year of assessment', 'Only applicable from the 2008 year of assessment', 'SARS PAYE BRS - PAYE Employer Reconciliation V23.0.0 (effective 1 March 2024; PDF sha256 220bf3ac4e13f5ffb0e8f4d090071db1babdcfec2425c5c5526d74d509e350ca); row text carried from the SARS PAYE-AE-06-G06 (Guide for Codes Applicable to Employees Tax Certificates 2026) 2026 list (no change in meaning for this code)', 'https://www.sars.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/Docs/PAYE/BRS/SARS_PAYE_BRS-PAYE-Employer-Reconciliation_V23-0-0.pdf', '• Lump sum payments accruing after 1 October 2007 from a fund termination of (pension/pension preservation/retirement annuity/provident/ provident employment preservation fund) in respect of retirement or death. lump sum benefits / • Lump sum payments accruing after 28 February 2009 from a Pension or Commutation of Provident Fund in respect of termination of services per sub paragraph annuities 2(1)(a)((ii)(AA) or (BB) of the Second Schedule of the Income Tax Act (e.g. (Subject to retrenchment)', 'v23.0.0'),
  ('3920', 2025, 'lump_sum', 'Lump sum withdrawal benefits (PAYE)', 'active', NULL, '3920', NULL, NULL, 'SARS PAYE BRS - PAYE Employer Reconciliation V23.0.0 (effective 1 March 2024; PDF sha256 220bf3ac4e13f5ffb0e8f4d090071db1babdcfec2425c5c5526d74d509e350ca); row text carried from the SARS PAYE-AE-06-G06 (Guide for Codes Applicable to Employees Tax Certificates 2026) 2026 list (no change in meaning for this code)', 'https://www.sars.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/Docs/PAYE/BRS/SARS_PAYE_BRS-PAYE-Employer-Reconciliation_V23-0-0.pdf', '• Lump sum payments accruing after 28 February 2009 from a Pension/ withdrawal Pension preservation/Retirement annuity/Provident/provident preservation benefits fund in respect of withdrawal (e.g. resignation, transfer, divorce, housing loan (Subject to payments, immigration withdrawal, withdrawal due to visa expiry, etc.). PAYE) Insurers must also use this code where there is a transfer from a living annuity to another living annuity. Note: ▫ With effect from 2010 year of assessment, amounts pr', 'v23.0.0'),
  ('3921', 2025, 'lump_sum', 'Living annuity', 'active', NULL, '3921', NULL, NULL, 'SARS PAYE BRS - PAYE Employer Reconciliation V23.0.0 (effective 1 March 2024; PDF sha256 220bf3ac4e13f5ffb0e8f4d090071db1babdcfec2425c5c5526d74d509e350ca); row text carried from the SARS PAYE-AE-06-G06 (Guide for Codes Applicable to Employees Tax Certificates 2026) 2026 list (no change in meaning for this code)', 'https://www.sars.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/Docs/PAYE/BRS/SARS_PAYE_BRS-PAYE-Employer-Reconciliation_V23-0-0.pdf', '• Lump sum payments accruing after 28 February 2009 from a and section 15C pension/pension/preservation/retirementannuity/provident/provident of the Pension preservation fund in respect of withdrawal due to: Funds Act, ▫ Surplus apportionments paid in terms of section 15C of the Pension surplus Funds Act of 1956; apportionments ▫ Withdrawal after retirement from a living annuity in terms of paragraph (c) (Subject to of the definition of living annuity, where the value of the assets become PAYE)', 'v23.0.0'),
  ('3922', 2025, 'lump_sum', 'Compensation', 'conditional', NULL, '3922', 'valid from 2012 year of', NULL, 'SARS PAYE BRS - PAYE Employer Reconciliation V23.0.0 (effective 1 March 2024; PDF sha256 220bf3ac4e13f5ffb0e8f4d090071db1babdcfec2425c5c5526d74d509e350ca); row text carried from the SARS PAYE-AE-06-G06 (Guide for Codes Applicable to Employees Tax Certificates 2026) 2026 list (no change in meaning for this code)', 'https://www.sars.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/Docs/PAYE/BRS/SARS_PAYE_BRS-PAYE-Employer-Reconciliation_V23-0-0.pdf', '• Lump sum payments accruing after 01 March 2011 from a compensation i.e., death fund in respect of withdrawal due to: during ▫ Withdrawal after death from a compensation fund in terms of Section employment 10(1)(gB)(iii) of the definition of compensation fund, as prescribed by the (Excl./PAYE) Minister in the Gazette; ▫ Code is applicable to all transaction years. Note: ▫ Codes 3922 are mandatory if code 4115 is specified; ▫ Must be included in this code (3922) and is only valid from 2012 year', 'v23.0.0'),
  ('3923', 2025, 'lump_sum', 'Transfer of Unclaimed Benefits (PAYE)', 'conditional', NULL, '3923', 'Applicable from 2018 to 2024 Year of Assessment | applicable from 2018 to 2024 year of assessment', 'Only applicable from 2018 to 2024 year of assessment', 'SARS PAYE BRS - PAYE Employer Reconciliation V23.0.0 (effective 1 March 2024; PDF sha256 220bf3ac4e13f5ffb0e8f4d090071db1babdcfec2425c5c5526d74d509e350ca); row text carried from the SARS PAYE-AE-06-G06 (Guide for Codes Applicable to Employees Tax Certificates 2026) 2026 list (no change in meaning for this code)', 'https://www.sars.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/Docs/PAYE/BRS/SARS_PAYE_BRS-PAYE-Employer-Reconciliation_V23-0-0.pdf', '• Transfer of Unclaimed Benefits (as per the Pension Fund Act No. 24 of 1956) Unclaimed not yet claimed and transferred to an unclaimed preservation fund. Benefits Note: ▫ Funds are not required to submit IRP5 certificates for the transfers of inactive member benefits where the fund does not have sufficient information. ▫ Applicable from 2018 to 2024 Year of Assessment.', 'v23.0.0'),
  ('3924', 2025, 'lump_sum', 'Transfer on Retirement (PAYE)', 'conditional', NULL, '3924', 'Applicable from 2019 Year of Assessment | applicable from 2019 year of assessment', 'Only applicable from 2019 year of assessment', 'SARS PAYE BRS - PAYE Employer Reconciliation V23.0.0 (effective 1 March 2024; PDF sha256 220bf3ac4e13f5ffb0e8f4d090071db1babdcfec2425c5c5526d74d509e350ca); row text carried from the SARS PAYE-AE-06-G06 (Guide for Codes Applicable to Employees Tax Certificates 2026) 2026 list (no change in meaning for this code)', 'https://www.sars.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/Docs/PAYE/BRS/SARS_PAYE_BRS-PAYE-Employer-Reconciliation_V23-0-0.pdf', '• Transfer of a retirement benefit on or after normal retirement age as defined retirement in the rules of the fund but before retirement date (i.e., in terms of Par.2 (PAYE) (1)(c) of the Second Schedule to the Income Tax Act. • This is applicable for a transfer from a Pension or Provident fund to Retirement Annuity Fund. Note: ▫ Applicable from 2019 Year of Assessment.', 'v23.0.0'),
  ('3926', 2025, 'lump_sum', 'Savings withdrawal benefit (PAYE)', 'conditional', NULL, '3926', 'Applicable from 2025 Year of Assessment | applicable from 2025 year of assessment Codes', 'Only applicable from 2025 year of assessment Codes', 'SARS PAYE BRS - PAYE Employer Reconciliation V23.0.0 (effective 1 March 2024; PDF sha256 220bf3ac4e13f5ffb0e8f4d090071db1babdcfec2425c5c5526d74d509e350ca); row text carried from the SARS PAYE-AE-06-G06 (Guide for Codes Applicable to Employees Tax Certificates 2026) 2026 list (no change in meaning for this code)', 'https://www.sars.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/Docs/PAYE/BRS/SARS_PAYE_BRS-PAYE-Employer-Reconciliation_V23-0-0.pdf', '• Withdrawal from a Retirement Fund from the Savings Component / Pot withdrawal benefit (PAYE) ▫ As per definitions of “pension fund”, “pension preservation fund” “provident fund” “provident preservation fund” and “retirement annuity fund” in section 1(1) of the Income Tax Act ▫ Paragraph 2(1)(d) of the Second Schedule ▫ Paragraph 6B of the Second Schedule ▫ Definition of “savings withdrawal benefit” read with paragraph (‘eD) of the definition of “gross income” in section 1(1) of the Income Tax', 'v23.0.0'),
